     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **The order:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **The usual limit:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single dose is typically 500\u20131,000 mg. This order is about twice the daily maximum.\n- **Why it matters:** an overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Possible intended doses:**\n- 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided into 2 or 3 doses (for example 850 mg twice daily).\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it."
      }
     ],
